HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_4829e4e0, "with two copies of one place landing back on it the call's answer would depend on the copy-out order, and that is what `no aliasing exists among the values this language owns` rules out (panel 010)");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_359f041d, "pass a copy for one of them: declare a second cell holding the same value, pass `@` that cell, and write it back after the call");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_56ce4c16, "or make the two places different: distinct fields (`@p.x` and `@p.y`) and distinct literal indices (`@xs[0]` and `@xs[1]`) are accepted");
