HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_198b5b1e, "` on ");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_53671c, " is a word nothing reads: ");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_5fa4a519, " reaches no handle, so no rule can say which call hands the value over or takes it back, and the word could be false without anything noticing");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_1e02a775, "the marks are read on a handle \342\200\224 a group `record` with a `tag` and no fields \342\200\224 and on a value reaching one through its fields. Name the C type the pointer stands for and mark that: `record Block tag void` is C's `void *`, `record AI tag addrinfo` is `struct addrinfo *`, and the compiler writes `struct` where the header needs it");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_c993728, "on a handle the word does work: `acquires` must name an `extern` that takes one back with `consumes`, `consumes` refuses a value the caller only borrowed, and a handle nobody gives back aborts when `main` returns, naming its address. On a `ptr` none of that can happen, and a wrong word there was measured to free memory `malloc` never gave");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_4fd9a3d1, "this node has no written type");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_19b88e88, "no extern of this program takes one back");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_8beab37, ", at ");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_3cffd663, "hands back a `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_7db17313, "` inside `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_4c23e1f7, "unmarked_handle_producer");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_3140, "` ");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_3b51e2b3, " and does not say whether the program owes it \342\200\224 `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_7acff04b, "` takes one back");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_6a7da702, ", so this binding has said how a `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_776aaacd, "` ends and not how it begins");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_4c917f25, "write `acquires ");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_51cfbb32, "` if the call gives the handle away and the program must return it, or `borrows` if the library keeps it and the program owes nothing. No C header states which, so the binding author states it: `sqlite3_prepare_v2` gives a statement and `sqlite3_next_stmt` lends one, and their C signatures are the same shape");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_e815a81, "one mark answers for the whole value, however many handles it carries: C frees a composite with one call, and `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_6da60f9e, "` is only where the first one sits");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_6d7ce9, "unread_releaser");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_6a5e13f3, "` does not end a `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_2b8f21b7, "`'s life: no `extern` of this module declares it taking one back with `consumes`");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_665d27d, "`acquires` names the call that ENDS what this one begins, so the name has to be an `extern` in this module with a `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_646e48e1, "` parameter marked `consumes`. Declare it, or write `borrows` if the library keeps the handle and the program owes nothing");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_24abd5d8, "`str`");
